1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
In Ecuador's public schools, news about
a child travels on a scrap of paper.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
WhatsApp groups?

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:14,000
One school banned them: “they were
taking the teachers' numbers.”

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Teachers are left exposed, and
families find out too late.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Cresco is a safe bridge
between school and family.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
The teacher writes down what
happened, in her own words.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,000
The behaviour score updates on its own.

8
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:39,000
The family gets it instantly. The
notification never names the child.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Disagree? She disputes it in
writing, under her own name.

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,000
There are no anonymous messages in Cresco.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The teacher has 30 days
to answer in writing:

12
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
keep the entry, change it, or annul it.

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,000
If she annuls it, the score is
recalculated, and it all stays on record.

14
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
To talk, the family books a slot
in the teacher's office hours.

15
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
She confirms, and never
has to give out her number.

16
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:22,000
The essentials are free. Premium
appears only when a family wants more.

17
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,000
The purchase goes through RevenueCat,

18
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,000
and its webhook tells our
server to unlock the plan.

19
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,000
More history, a PDF report, and no ads.

20
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Teachers with several classes
get their own PRO plan.

21
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Everything in writing. No one anonymous.
Teachers never give out their number.

22
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Cresco: so no warning
sign arrives too late.
